! Water wB97X-D / STO-3G: geometry optimization regression  (v0.88.1)
!
! Phase-2 exercise for the wB97 family in one job: the analytic
! range-separated gradient (regular pass + erf-attenuated exchange-
! only pass, -beta*dK_lr/dA) drives the optimizer, and the built-in
! CHG damped dispersion of wB97X-D [Chai, Head-Gordon, PCCP 10, 6615
! (2008)] contributes to both the energy and the gradient at every
! step:
!     E_disp = - sum_{A<B} C6_AB/R^6 / (1 + 6 (R/R_r)^-12) ,
! Grimme D2 C6 / vdW radii, verified against the CP2K reference
! implementation (see BENCHMARK_NOTES_v0.88.1.md).
!
! Reference values (1 thread, default grid; bit-reproducibility
! references, see the grid note in test_v088_h2o_wb97x.inp):
!
!   Optimization converged in 5 steps.
!   Final energy:  -75.316369054469 Ha
!
! ERRATUM (v0.88.2): the original v0.88.1 reference here
! (-75.326187295606) was polluted by the attenuated-ERI-store
! geometry-caching bug (see the v0.88.2 changelog): every SCF after
! the first optimization step reused the FIRST geometry's K_lr
! integrals.  The corrected optimum is confirmed against
! PySCF/libxc + an independent CHG evaluation to 1.2e-6 Ha on
! converged grids (BENCHMARK_NOTES_v0.88.2.md).
!
! Gradient validation summary for this functional (v0.88.1 battery):
! analytic vs central-difference of the FINAL total energy (i.e.
! including the dispersion term) agrees to 1.3e-7 Ha/bohr on the
! distorted-water probe; the CHG pair term alone matches an
! independent python evaluation to all printed digits.
%method  WB97X-D
%basis   sto-3g
%job     opt
%charge  0
%mult    1
%geom angstrom
O    0.000000    0.000000    0.117300
H    0.000000    0.757200   -0.469200
H    0.000000   -0.757200   -0.469200
*end
